WEBVTT

00:05.269 --> 00:11.174
Dareni mo mienu deshou

00:13.010 --> 00:18.505
Me o tojite kimi o omou

00:19.150 --> 00:24.918
Itsuka de au

00:25.256 --> 00:31.354
Kaze no hana yo, Saa hiraku no yo

00:31.662 --> 00:38.158
Watashi no kono me ni haru o misete

00:38.436 --> 00:44.568
Kaze no hana yo, Saa hiraku no yo

00:44.842 --> 00:51.111
Sayonara fuyu no machi

00:51.415 --> 00:57.650
Kaze no hana yo, Saa hiraku no yo

00:57.922 --> 01:04.384
Watashi no kokoro ni haru o yonde

01:04.695 --> 01:10.835
Kaze no hana yo, Saa hiraku no yo

01:10.835 --> 01:18.207
Sayonara yukitachi yo

01:32.957 --> 01:33.791
Preparing to Open

01:33.791 --> 01:36.521
Preparing to Open
All aboard! Departure time!

01:37.495 --> 01:39.163
- Go, go! Whee!

01:39.163 --> 01:41.256
- Go, go! Whee!
- Next stop, Meidai-mae. Meidai-mae!

01:41.766 --> 01:43.063
Watch out!

01:43.100 --> 01:44.829
Those of you transferring,
please proceed to the gate.

01:46.070 --> 01:49.907
The request for tonight
may take a while...

01:49.907 --> 01:51.309
Aye-aye, Captain!

01:51.309 --> 01:53.743
Good ol' Oyamada,
you're so cool!

01:54.345 --> 01:57.582
Thank you very much.
Yume, shall we get going now?

01:57.582 --> 01:58.640
Yes.

01:59.383 --> 02:00.718
And there you have it.

02:00.718 --> 02:01.946
Now, onto other news...

02:04.422 --> 02:05.690
Are you all right?

02:05.690 --> 02:09.285
Yes. I'm sorry
to worry you.

02:09.627 --> 02:10.328
- Then let's go.

02:10.328 --> 02:11.696
- Then let's go.
- This afternoon...

02:11.696 --> 02:14.065
River Disaster: Three children drowned
This afternoon, a drowning accident
in Okutama, Tokyo,

02:14.065 --> 02:16.932
River Disaster: Three children drowned
claimed the lives of three children,
all caught in a flooded river.

02:17.301 --> 02:23.741
The children all belong to a local orphanage,
Takebayashi Gakuen, in Setagaya.

02:23.741 --> 02:27.609
The three were rescued
and taken to the hospital.

02:28.145 --> 02:33.139
"I Want to Be a Mage"

02:33.851 --> 02:35.318
Tama River flooded. 3 children drowned.
1 in critical condition

02:35.353 --> 02:36.254
Live from Kawashima Hospital.

02:36.254 --> 02:41.525
Live from Kawashima Hospital.
I'm now in front of the hospital.
Two children have recuperated,

02:41.525 --> 02:43.459
Critical Condition:
Nishihara, Yuta, Age 5.
but one remains in a coma
in very critical condition...

02:52.169 --> 02:55.570
Preparing to Open

02:56.073 --> 02:59.176
Where in the world
did Big Brother Kera go?

02:59.176 --> 03:01.167
He's just like a kite
with a broken string.

03:01.379 --> 03:05.645
There's nothing we can do now.
I'll open the bar when I get back.

03:08.052 --> 03:09.952
Hola! Como estas?

03:23.901 --> 03:26.971
Kera! Are you all right?
What happened?

03:26.971 --> 03:30.873
Milinda-san, sorry for
the trouble. I'll take over...

03:54.966 --> 03:57.025
Did something happen
at the orphanage?

03:57.234 --> 03:58.069
Or, uh...

03:58.069 --> 04:00.401
No, that's not it.
It's nothing.

04:00.972 --> 04:03.236
I'm here to listen.

04:13.017 --> 04:14.251
Milinda-san!
You're still in your uni...

04:14.251 --> 04:15.252
Is Kera here?

04:15.252 --> 04:17.413
Yes. He's talking
to Oyamada-sensei.

04:17.521 --> 04:20.422
Ugh! What's he
doing on his own?

04:23.294 --> 04:26.430
I told you I'd come with you
to talk to Masami-chan!

04:26.430 --> 04:27.590
I can talk to him by myself!

04:27.732 --> 04:30.895
Milinda, did you sneak
away from work?

04:31.035 --> 04:34.505
That's right.
So, did you tell him?

04:34.505 --> 04:36.268
Um, not just yet...

04:38.075 --> 04:39.235
Yes.

04:40.177 --> 04:44.705
Oyamada-sensei, it's almost time
to leave for the request site.

04:44.949 --> 04:47.318
Uh, is it that time
already?

04:47.318 --> 04:50.719
See? Because you're dilly-dallying!
Do you want me to tell him?

04:50.955 --> 04:52.718
Milinda-san,
give me a break!

04:52.990 --> 04:55.151
I'll tell him myself!

04:57.094 --> 04:58.959
Kera, how long
have you been here?

04:59.163 --> 05:00.152
About two years.

05:00.498 --> 05:05.128
During that time, you couldn't tell
anything to Masami-chan by yourself.

05:06.003 --> 05:08.471
What in the world
are you talking about?

05:08.639 --> 05:10.539
There's no telling
what Fate will bring.

05:11.075 --> 05:13.134
You may die tomorrow.

05:13.344 --> 05:16.472
Life's too short for hesitation!

05:19.116 --> 05:23.687
I'm sorry if
I'm being rough, but...

05:23.687 --> 05:25.211
Milinda-san, that's enough...

05:26.057 --> 05:28.821
Hey, Kera! Let me go!

05:40.671 --> 05:42.798
I'm not gonna apologize.

05:46.777 --> 05:51.082
Hmph! Until you understand that
it's ok to occasionally depend on

05:51.082 --> 05:54.347
someone or trouble them,
I'll keep being pushy and forceful.

05:56.554 --> 05:56.921
- Uh...

05:56.921 --> 05:58.513
- Uh...
- Your break-time's over.

05:58.689 --> 05:59.678
Huh?

06:01.992 --> 06:03.357
See you later!

07:13.564 --> 07:14.258
I'm back!

07:14.932 --> 07:18.595
The bar's shopping list
was just mint leaves. Uh!

07:19.603 --> 07:21.594
I'm sorry to have startled you.

07:22.239 --> 07:26.608
Um, that's...
a ring of a retired mage...

07:26.777 --> 07:28.438
Mages...

07:29.446 --> 07:32.745
Mages use their rings
to exercise power, right?

07:33.017 --> 07:33.346
No.

07:34.285 --> 07:36.276
Then how do you use power?

07:36.620 --> 07:38.055
- By our own power.

07:38.055 --> 07:40.148
- By our own power.
- Then, what about the rings?

07:40.291 --> 07:42.623
They're for ID and things.

07:47.464 --> 07:50.627
If I had this, I thought
I could use Special Power.

07:51.235 --> 07:52.634
What do you mean?

07:54.271 --> 07:56.296
Temptation came over me...

07:57.007 --> 08:02.646
I saw it in Boss' desk. I just
borrowed it. I'd return it soon.

08:02.646 --> 08:04.807
No! I stole it! I...

08:05.382 --> 08:06.644
Why?

08:07.284 --> 08:09.650
I thought I might be able
to use Special Power.

08:09.787 --> 08:12.654
If it's Special Power,
Oyamada-sensei or I can...

08:13.157 --> 08:16.649
That's not the point.
I want to be a mage!

08:17.561 --> 08:19.324
Become a mage?

08:19.730 --> 08:24.224
That's right.
I... I want to become a mage!

08:37.014 --> 08:40.973
Kawashima Hospital

08:43.487 --> 08:51.189
Those of you whose numbers are displayed,
please come pick up your prescriptions.

09:04.041 --> 09:06.771
Room 505
Nishihara, Yuta

09:10.714 --> 09:11.703
Yes?

09:12.916 --> 09:16.443
How is Yuta's condition?

09:20.257 --> 09:22.748
You can't become a mage
with Special Power.

09:23.127 --> 09:25.696
Even Special Power
can't do that.

09:25.696 --> 09:28.722
Then, how can I become a mage?

09:29.099 --> 09:34.469
You just don't become a mage.
You have to be born one. So...

09:35.239 --> 09:37.400
You have to be born one?

09:39.576 --> 09:40.736
Ugh...

09:41.745 --> 09:44.908
Kera-san, why do you
want to become a mage?

09:46.150 --> 09:52.749
Yume, you have a home and parents.
They are as natural as breathing air, right?

09:53.357 --> 09:54.016
Right.

09:54.958 --> 09:58.758
I wanted to grow up
in a home, too.

09:58.929 --> 10:06.437
Kids want to grow up protected
by their own gentle, loving parents.

10:06.437 --> 10:10.601
But we didn't have that.

10:11.408 --> 10:17.938
That's why we're so desperate to find
something precious to use as our support.

10:18.382 --> 10:21.943
If I could tell others I'm a mage,
that'd be pretty cool, wouldn't it?

10:26.623 --> 10:28.784
Everyone calls him
"Kera" now.

10:29.259 --> 10:31.318
Kera! Kato-kun?

10:31.595 --> 10:33.961
Because he has
such a cute smile.

10:34.164 --> 10:40.104
Is that so? Kato-kun grew
up to be a fine young man.

10:40.104 --> 10:43.801
He met such
a nice person like you.

10:43.841 --> 10:47.811
He's always concerned about
the children at the orphanage.

10:47.811 --> 10:51.872
When he heard about Yuta's
accident, he called right away.

10:56.653 --> 11:01.058
I wanted to become a mage
who specializes in children.

11:01.058 --> 11:03.219
For the sake of the children...

11:05.763 --> 11:07.628
Preparing to Open

11:12.469 --> 11:14.596
Would you like
to give it a try?

11:14.872 --> 11:16.169
Give it a try?

11:16.440 --> 11:20.577
The ring that I'm wearing
reacts to Special Power,

11:20.577 --> 11:23.842
but the hologram can only be
produced by me, the registered owner.

11:24.348 --> 11:25.838
It reacts?
In what way?

11:26.150 --> 11:27.050
- It sparkles.

11:27.050 --> 11:28.677
- It sparkles.
- So, what should I do?

11:28.852 --> 11:32.583
Just create water or fire.
A thing is fine, too.

11:32.723 --> 11:35.959
Or you could disappear
or fly in the sky.

11:35.959 --> 11:37.358
Use Special Power.

11:37.795 --> 11:39.729
That's easy for YOU to say!

11:43.000 --> 11:44.194
That's not it!

11:44.468 --> 11:48.199
Use your Special Power.
Please don't pray or recite.

11:51.041 --> 11:54.704
Kawashima Hospital

11:59.550 --> 12:02.883
I can't do it!
No matter how hard I try...

12:04.388 --> 12:06.788
I'm sorry.
I was outside listening.

12:07.057 --> 12:08.388
Boss...

12:12.529 --> 12:14.898
Was it too hard
to talk to me?

12:14.898 --> 12:16.889
No, it's not that.

12:17.067 --> 12:23.233
If I came to you, you'd have known
right away if I was a mage or not. Right?

12:25.476 --> 12:26.272
Probably.

12:26.510 --> 12:28.846
I was scared to hear you
tell me I wasn't a mage.

12:28.846 --> 12:31.178
That's why I couldn't
come to you...

12:35.152 --> 12:38.918
A boy from my orphanage
was in that accident at the river.

12:39.490 --> 12:43.727
If I were a mage, I might
be able to help him.

12:43.727 --> 12:48.926
Maybe I could help more
and more suffering children.

12:49.600 --> 12:51.932
That's what I thought, anyway.

12:52.202 --> 12:57.774
Kera, Special Power
can only do a little.

12:57.774 --> 12:58.934
Special Power is not almighty.

13:00.277 --> 13:04.441
You're right.
But I... just hoped...

13:07.618 --> 13:08.277
Yes.

13:14.558 --> 13:19.518
Kawashima Hospital

13:37.281 --> 13:37.981
- Yuta.

13:37.981 --> 13:39.312
- Yuta.
- You came for him.

13:39.516 --> 13:42.152
Headmaster!
Are you all right?

13:42.152 --> 13:43.987
I'm fine.

13:43.987 --> 13:47.980
Yuta-kun, Big Brother Go
has come to see you.

13:48.659 --> 13:49.751
Yuta!

13:50.027 --> 13:54.164
When you get all better,
I'll take you wherever you like.

13:54.164 --> 13:55.188
So, hang in there!

14:06.610 --> 14:08.745
Why don't you go home?

14:08.745 --> 14:09.473
No.

14:09.646 --> 14:11.614
Please don't overdo it.

14:13.650 --> 14:16.186
- Boss, please save Yuta's life!

14:16.186 --> 14:17.016
- Boss, please save Yuta's life!
- Save his life?

14:17.220 --> 14:18.522
He's only 5 years old!

14:18.522 --> 14:21.992
If he dies now, there's
no point to his being born!

14:21.992 --> 14:24.153
I'm begging you.
Use your Special Power!

14:24.361 --> 14:27.762
Oyamada-sensei,
isn't there anything we can do?

14:28.398 --> 14:32.903
If pain needs to be relieved,
the hospital mage will come.

14:32.903 --> 14:37.441
Pain? It's not that! I want you to save
Yuta's life with your Special Power!

14:37.441 --> 14:39.743
Even Special Power can't do that.

14:39.743 --> 14:40.368
But...

14:40.410 --> 14:44.039
If I could,
I would have already.

14:44.481 --> 14:47.917
If I could, I would have
done it a long time ago...

14:50.253 --> 14:53.490
Actually, I don't do well
at hospitals.

14:53.490 --> 14:55.253
I'll be in the lobby
for a while.

14:55.726 --> 14:57.057
Yes.

15:14.344 --> 15:19.680
Kawashima Hospital

15:30.260 --> 15:33.463
That's right. You liked
all kinds of vehicles, right?

15:33.463 --> 15:35.954
I'll collect commemorative
stamps with you.

15:36.199 --> 15:39.100
We'll ride the train and
the subway all day long.

15:39.603 --> 15:40.934
You wanna ride
the bus, too?

15:43.540 --> 15:43.940
Room 505
Nishihara, Yuta

15:43.940 --> 15:45.931
Room 505
Nishihara, Yuta
And we'll go to a
baseball game, too.

15:46.276 --> 15:49.939
It's nice and cool at Jingu Stadium
with the summer breeze at night.

15:50.247 --> 15:53.150
After the ball game, you can
spend the night at my place.

15:53.150 --> 15:55.948
My bathroom's small,
but it's my own.

15:56.119 --> 15:58.451
And I'll get you
your own pair of pajamas, Yuta.

16:07.197 --> 16:08.632
I understand.

16:08.632 --> 16:10.122
Milinda-san...

16:10.233 --> 16:15.136
Let's stay here by
his side and root for him.

16:17.407 --> 16:18.135
Right.

16:27.150 --> 16:29.986
Hey, and we'll carry
a portable shrine on our shoulders.

16:29.986 --> 16:31.822
We'll yell real loud,
and that'll feel good!

16:31.822 --> 16:34.558
And... And then,
in the summer...

16:34.558 --> 16:37.060
You'll get up early in
the morning to catch beetles?

16:37.060 --> 16:40.097
Uh, yeah!
Beetles... Great!

16:40.097 --> 16:43.066
The male beetles' horns
are awesome, aren't they?

16:43.500 --> 16:48.672
Yuta-kun, summer's just starting.
Have you had any snow cones yet?

16:48.672 --> 16:52.335
Or watermelon? I'll gladly teach you
anything, like catching cicadas.

16:52.743 --> 16:57.481
And a little tip for taking a summer nap
is to listen to the sound of wind chimes.

16:57.481 --> 16:59.346
It makes you feel good...

17:02.085 --> 17:04.178
Yuta! What's wrong?
Are you in pain?

17:04.855 --> 17:06.186
It's the wind chimes.

17:07.257 --> 17:09.555
It's because he heard you say
"wind chimes," I'm sure.

17:09.926 --> 17:11.188
Wind chimes?

17:11.561 --> 17:14.860
Yuta's mother bought him a wind chime
on their way to our school.

17:15.599 --> 17:17.534
They're Yuta's keepsake
of his mother.

17:17.534 --> 17:19.195
Where is it now?

17:19.236 --> 17:22.694
It was... It broke.

17:26.510 --> 17:28.205
Wind chimes...

17:37.654 --> 17:40.791
All right! We'll go buy
wind chimes together.

17:40.791 --> 17:43.885
What kind do you like?
I don't know much about wind chimes.

17:44.094 --> 17:47.655
You've got to tell me!
Ok? I'm begging you!

17:55.639 --> 17:56.401
Yuta!

18:01.178 --> 18:02.236
What's the matter?

18:02.379 --> 18:04.244
Hurry! Please hurry!!

18:04.581 --> 18:10.720
Yuta, wait! We're gonna go buy
wind chimes, right? Yuta! Yuta!

18:10.720 --> 18:12.950
YUTAAAA!!

18:44.187 --> 18:45.119
Yume...

18:47.557 --> 18:49.616
Then what in the world...

18:55.332 --> 18:57.300
Did I?

18:58.969 --> 19:02.302
Yuta! Look! Wind chimes!
They're everywhere!

19:02.806 --> 19:04.296
Now, wake up, Yuta!

19:04.774 --> 19:08.301
They're so beautiful!
Come on, take a look!

19:13.917 --> 19:15.179
Yuta.

19:19.489 --> 19:23.827
Oyamada-sensei! Kera-san's
Special Power! It's amazing! It's Yuta-kun!

19:23.827 --> 19:24.555
What?

19:32.869 --> 19:34.336
This is...

20:51.681 --> 20:55.785
I have to apologize
for stealing...

20:55.785 --> 20:57.120
It's yours now.

20:57.120 --> 20:59.418
What? This ring's
very special to you.

21:00.323 --> 21:02.416
That's why I'm giving it to you.

21:19.976 --> 21:26.609
Furikaereba ima demo soko ni

21:29.619 --> 21:35.956
Oikaketeta mirai ga atta

21:37.861 --> 21:46.826
Boku no kokoro ni aru taisetsu na mono

21:47.203 --> 21:51.640
Mada mienai ao to

21:52.809 --> 21:59.305
Nagareru kumo ni negatta

22:02.485 --> 22:04.320
Under the Blue Sky

22:04.320 --> 22:11.761
Ano hi bokura ga egaita yume kara

22:11.761 --> 22:18.667
Samenai you ni tomaranai you ni

22:21.337 --> 22:23.396
Under the Blue Sky

22:23.740 --> 22:30.202
Kagayaki nagara aruiteikou yo

22:30.747 --> 22:37.585
Owaranai tabi wa tsuzuku

22:49.432 --> 22:50.767
PREVIEW

22:50.767 --> 22:51.893
PREVIEW
All right! Now I'm
finally one of the mages!

22:51.935 --> 22:53.803
All right! Now I'm
finally one of the mages!

22:53.803 --> 22:55.538
Oh, no. You have
a long way to go.

22:55.538 --> 22:56.172
What?

22:56.172 --> 22:58.575
First, you need to register at
the nearby Office of Mage Labor.

22:58.575 --> 23:00.143
Then you take a test
on basic mage knowledge

23:00.143 --> 23:02.145
and have your Special Power
evaluated.

23:02.145 --> 23:02.879
What?
Are you serious?

23:02.879 --> 23:06.249
The evaluation is really tough...

23:06.249 --> 23:06.816
Ugh...

23:06.816 --> 23:10.547
And the next evaluation
step is unbelievably weird. And, uh...

23:10.587 --> 23:10.787
"The Mage Who Couldn't Become a Mage"

23:10.787 --> 23:14.724
"The Mage Who Couldn't Become a Mage"
Episode 7 is "The Mage
Who Couldn't Become a Mage."

23:14.724 --> 23:15.925
"The Mage Who Couldn't Become a Mage"
I hope you look forward to it!

23:15.925 --> 23:19.292
"The Mage Who Couldn't Become a Mage"
Now it's getting really interesting!
